# `__SITE.md__` — Landscaping Template 4 (Cinematic Nightscape)

> Build type: **TEMPLATE**. Template Build Content Policy applies to every policy-governed section. The form ships in **preview mode** (`NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_MODE=preview`) — no Resend wiring runs end-to-end, ContactForm short-circuits at the client and renders the preview-launching message. All copy is generic lorem ipsum or policy-mandated placeholders. Form deliverability (`CLIENT_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL`, `CLIENT_BUSINESS_NAME`) intentionally blank — wired only at Phase 7 production migration.

## Variation lock (V3.4 — Black-Tie Speakeasy / Automotive Showroom)

**All-dark cinematic. Near-pure-black + champagne + DM Sans single-typeface.** Reference templates: Motorflow (Webflow automotive — `motorflowtemplate.webflow.io`) and Kitui Fluid (Squarespace fashion). Single-typeface system: **DM Sans 400/500/600/700** for both body AND display — display variant distinguished only by uppercase + `tracking-wide` letter-spacing + larger size. Mood comes from composition, not font personality. Near-pure-black backgrounds (`#0A0A0C` base / `#050607` deepest / `#1A1A1F` lifted), champagne accent (`#D4B679` solid / `#E8D4A3` glow) replacing the original cyan, ALL 10 sections dark with varied dark treatments (spotlight gradients on Hero/About/CTA, star-field decorative overlays on Services/Recent Work, lifted-midnight on Why Us, subtle gradient on Reviews/Footer/Recent Work). Mood vocabulary: shadowy, showy, dramatic, fancy, dim, premium-onyx, cinematic. V3.2 pivoted from V3.1's Big Shoulders Display — the condensed-architectural letterforms were "doing too much"; the single-typeface DM Sans approach lets the typography recede and the composition carry the elegance (Kitui Fluid's approach). V3.3 added **ambient background photography to every content section** (Services, WhyUs, FAQ, CtaSection, Footer), but the photos were invisible at opacity 0.10–0.22 against the 0.85–0.98 darkening overlay. V3.4 made the atmosphere actually VISIBLE: photo opacity raised to 0.30–0.40, darkening overlays dropped to 0.60–0.78, section base gradients varied perceptibly across the tone map (Services lifted-slate `#15151A`→`#0A0A0C`, WhyUs more-lifted-gray `#1F1F25`→`#0F0F14`, FAQ lifted-cool `#15151A`→`#080A0D`, CTA dramatic `#0A0A0C`→`#020203`, Footer abyss `#020203`→`#000000`), champagne radial glow blobs bumped from 0.03–0.05 → 0.08–0.12 opacity at 60–70% spread, noise overlay 0.04 → 0.06 site-wide. Scrolling through the page now reads as moving through visibly different rooms with different ambient lighting — fixing the "sections felt flat / nothing going on in the background" feedback from V3.3. This adds the textural depth missing from uniform dark gradients, matching Motorflow's automotive-silhouette-through-darkness DNA and Kitui Fluid's editorial-photography-as-ambient-texture pattern. Visually distinct from Templates 1 (earthy daylight), 2 (sage), 3 (industrial slate-yellow) — Template 4 is the cool/electric outlier turned all-dark luxury.

Three signature visual mechanics:

1. **Spotlight radial gradients on dark sections.** Hero, About, CTA — instead of flat dark bgs, a `radial-gradient(ellipse at center, midnight-lighter, midnight-darker)` overlay brightens the center where content sits and darkens to near-pure midnight at edges. Every spotlight section reads as "lit by a single overhead source."
2. **Glassmorphism on three signature elements** — Hero ContactForm card, Trust Strip, Mobile Sticky CTA Bar Call pill. `backdrop-blur-xl` + semi-transparent bg + subtle `ring-1` glass-edge. Not on every card — over-applied = loss of distinctiveness.
3. **Cyan glow on CTAs and the active carousel slide.** `shadow-[0_0_40px_rgba(34,211,238,0.4)]`-style glow on primary CTA buttons, active Recent Work slide, FAQ open item, Quote pill. The architectural-lighting signal — glowing edges where light sources sit.

## Section order (top to bottom)

1. Nav
2. Mobile Sticky CTA Bar (body-level mount; appears bottom of viewport on mobile only)
3. Hero
4. Trust Strip
5. Services
6. Reviews
7. Why Us
8. About
9. Recent Work
10. FAQ
11. CTA Section
12. Footer

## Adjacency audit

Template 4 is **dark-dominant** — 5 of 10 main sections are dark + Footer makes 6. Light sections (Services, Reviews, Why Us, FAQ) act as visual breathers between dark slabs. Sequence: Hero(D-spotlight) → Trust(glass-over-dark) → Services(L) → Reviews(L-gray) → Why Us(L) → About(D-spotlight) → Recent Work(D-deepest) → FAQ(L) → CTA(D-spotlight) → Footer(D-deepest).

| From → To | Tones | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Hero → Trust Strip | DARK-spotlight → glass-over-DARK | Trust Strip overlaps Hero's lower edge via negative margin-top, so the "transition" is actually a visual extension of Hero with the Trust Strip floating above. No flat-vs-flat adjacency. |
| Trust Strip → Services | DARK → LIGHT-slate-50 | Natural alternation. |
| Services → Reviews | SLATE-50 → WHITE | Subtle tonal flip; supports section break. |
| Reviews → Why Us | WHITE → SLATE-50 | Subtle tonal flip. |
| Why Us → About | LIGHT → DARK-spotlight | Natural alternation. |
| About → Recent Work | DARK-spotlight → DARK-deepest-flat | About's spotlight has visible center-brightening; Recent Work is the deepest near-black with star-field overlay + bright carousel imagery — two different dark treatments, not flat-vs-flat. |
| Recent Work → FAQ | DARK → LIGHT | Natural alternation. |
| FAQ → CTA Section | LIGHT → DARK-spotlight | Natural alternation. |
| CTA Section → Footer | DARK-spotlight → DARK-deepest-flat | **Mitigation:** Footer wrapper gets `border-t border-t-cyan-400/30` — thin cyan hairline divider, the same role the safety-yellow hairline plays on Template 3. |

---

## Nav

- **Architecture:** Fixed, transparent-at-top, scroll-driven (per `transparent-navbar-prompt.md`, applied in Phase 3).
- **At-top state:** `bg-transparent` + white text/links. The cyan-glow Get Quote button retains its glow even at-top (the CTA never blends in — it's always the highest-contrast moment on the page). Variant: dark hero (Hero's bg is deep midnight + spotlight gradient).
- **Scrolled state (>16px):** `bg-[#0F1E3D]/95 backdrop-blur shadow-sm` + white text/links + cyan-glow Get Quote button (`bg-cyan-400 text-slate-900 shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(34,211,238,0.4)]`).
- **Brand mark:** Text-only `[Template 4]` in DM Serif Display weight 400 at `text-xl md:text-2xl`. **NO Lucide icon.**
- **Z-index:** `z-40` (above Mobile Sticky CTA Bar's `z-30`; mobile menu open covers the sticky bar).
- **Nav links:** Home, Services, About, Contact. Hash links via `<SmoothLink>` in Phase 3. At-top text-white; scrolled text-white (Navbar bg becomes opaque midnight so white still reads). Link hovers `hover:text-cyan-400`.
- **Mobile:** Hamburger menu slides open from top, covers viewport including sticky bar.

## Mobile Sticky CTA Bar

- **Mount:** Body level in `app/layout.tsx`, immediately after `<main className="pb-20 md:pb-0">{children}</main>`. NOT inside `<Navbar>`.
- **Implementation:** Wrapper structure, z-index ladder, safe-area inset (1rem floor), pointer-events rules — **verbatim from `mobile-sticky-cta-prompt.md`**. Only the visual treatment of the two pills changes for Template 4.
- **Visibility:** `md:hidden`. Wrapper `pointer-events: none`; each pill `pointer-events: auto`. `z-30`.
- **Call pill (secondary) — Template 4 glassmorphism override:**
  - Bg: `backdrop-blur-xl bg-white/20 ring-1 ring-white/30` instead of the standard solid white.
  - Text + icon: `text-white` (translucent pill over varied bg — white reads as long as the underlying section has sufficient contrast, which holds on every dark section the pill overlaps; the white/20 bg is enough to anchor the pill against the bright Services/FAQ light sections too).
  - Shadow: `shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.3)]` (pronounced shadow, not the standard `shadow-lg`).
  - Icon: Lucide Phone, `strokeWidth={2}`.
  - Href: `<a href="tel:+15551234567">` (raw `<a>` — `tel:` doesn't smooth-scroll).
- **Quote pill (primary) — Template 4 cyan-glow override:**
  - Bg: `bg-cyan-400 text-slate-900` (electric cyan with always-dark-text per WCAG — see Always-Dark-Text-on-Cyan Rule in `__DESIGN.md__`).
  - Glow shadow: `shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(34,211,238,0.5)]` — the signature cyan emission.
  - Icon: Sparkle or ChevronRight, `text-slate-900`, `strokeWidth={2}`.
  - Href: `<SmoothLink href="#quote">` (smooth-scroll system handles 96px navbar offset; matches Hero ContactForm card's `id="quote"`).
- **Layout:** Both pills `flex-1` equal-width.

## Hero

- **Tone:** DARK + spotlight radial gradient.
- **Composition:** **SIDE-BY-SIDE — text LEFT, ContactForm RIGHT.** Grid `grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr] gap-10 lg:gap-12 xl:gap-16 items-center`. Mobile collapses to stacked (text first, form below). Section uses `lg:min-h-screen` so the entire hero fits the desktop fold (above-the-fold form is the conversion priority).
  - **Why side-by-side, not centered single-column:** the kickoff prompt's "centered single-column" framing is overridden by `agency-context.md` Visual Hard Rule #1, which mandates text LEFT + form RIGHT for every build, no exceptions. Template 3 also ended up reversing its kickoff's centered framing for the same reason. The cinematic-nightscape treatment (spotlight bg, glassmorphism on form card, oversized display serif H1) sits cleanly inside the standard text-LEFT/form-RIGHT composition.
- **Vertical padding:** `pt-24 pb-12 md:pt-28 md:pb-16 lg:pt-28 lg:pb-20`.
- **Background (THREE-layer composition, bottom to top):**
  1. **Layer 1 — Unsplash bg image.** Subject: **twilight/dusk shot of a finished hardscape, lit pathway, paver patio at blue hour, or completed estate property under spotlight**. Subject confirmed PERSON-FREE / ANIMAL-FREE / LIVING-THING-FREE. HEAD-checks 200. Rendered via `<ImageWithFallback fill object-cover className="absolute inset-0" />`.
  2. **Layer 2 — Spotlight radial gradient overlay.** `bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_center,rgba(15,30,61,0.4)_0%,rgba(10,20,41,0.95)_100%)]` — brightens center to ~40% darkness over the image, darkens edges to ~95%. The atmospheric "single overhead light source" effect.
  3. **Layer 3 — `noise-overlay` div** (applied in Phase 3) — `opacity-[0.035] mix-blend-overlay`. CRITICAL to prevent the diagonal hairline on the dark mid-tone areas.
  - All three overlay layers are `absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none`.
- **LEFT column (text, max-w-xl):**
  1. **Accent bar:** `h-1 w-12 bg-cyan-400 rounded-full mb-4` — the cyan rule above the eyebrow per Visual Hard Rule #2.
  2. **Eyebrow:** uppercase tracking-wide, `text-cyan-400 text-xs md:text-sm font-semibold mb-3`.
  3. **H1 — the centerpiece:** DM Serif Display weight 400, `text-6xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl xl:text-9xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight`. **Bigger than every prior template.** Max 2 lines at every breakpoint. Generic lorem ipsum noun phrase. **One one-word color pop in `text-cyan-400`.** Inherits white from parent. The oversized display serif on the dramatic spotlight bg = "movie poster" feel.
  4. **Subhead:** DM Sans weight 400, `text-lg md:text-xl text-slate-300 max-w-lg mt-6`. 1–2 sentences lorem ipsum.
  5. **Trust pills:** max 3, horizontal flex row, `gap-2 md:gap-3 mt-8`. Pills: `bg-white/10 text-slate-200 ring-1 ring-white/20 backdrop-blur-sm px-3 py-1.5 md:px-4 md:py-2 text-xs md:text-sm rounded-full`. Lucide icons (`ShieldCheck`, `Hammer`, `Award`) in `text-cyan-400`.
- **RIGHT column (form) — GLASSMORPHISM card:**
  - Container: `w-full lg:max-w-md xl:max-w-lg lg:justify-self-end`.
  - **Glassmorphism treatment:** `backdrop-blur-xl bg-slate-900/40 ring-1 ring-white/20 rounded-2xl shadow-2xl p-6 md:p-8`. The spotlight-lit Hero bg is visible through the card but blurred and darkened — visually anchors the form as "a frosted glass panel floating on a dramatic backdrop."
  - Form wrapper `id="quote"` (matches Mobile Sticky CTA Bar Quote pill).
  - Card eyebrow: small `text-cyan-400 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide font-semibold mb-2`. Card heading: DM Serif Display weight 400, `text-xl md:text-2xl text-white mb-1`. Card subhead: DM Sans `text-sm text-slate-400 mb-6`.
  - Form labels: DM Sans weight 500, `text-slate-300 text-sm`.
  - Inputs: `bg-slate-900/60 text-white border border-white/10 placeholder-slate-500 rounded-lg`. Min `text-base` (16px) to prevent iOS zoom-on-focus.
  - Submit button: `bg-cyan-400 text-slate-900 font-bold hover:bg-cyan-300 shadow-[0_0_40px_rgba(34,211,238,0.4)] hover:shadow-[0_0_60px_rgba(34,211,238,0.6)] transition-shadow duration-300`. **The cyan-glow CTA — the highest-contrast moment in the entire Hero.**
  - Honeypot field (hidden) per `resend-form-prompt.md` spec.
- **NO promo bar.**

## Trust Strip

- **Tone:** GLASSMORPHISM over Hero's lower edge.
- **Architecture:** Sits at the visual bottom of the Hero section, overlapping it via `position: relative; margin-top: -4rem; z-10` on a container that wraps a glass pill row.
- **Container:** `mx-auto max-w-6xl backdrop-blur-xl bg-white/10 ring-1 ring-white/20 rounded-2xl shadow-[0_24px_60px_-12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)] border-t-2 border-t-cyan-400/60 px-4 py-6 md:px-8 md:py-8`.
  - The `border-t-2 border-t-cyan-400/60` is the 2px cyan top border per Visual Hard Rule #2.
- **Layout:** Horizontal flex on desktop (`md:flex md:flex-row md:justify-between md:items-center`), 2-per-row grid on mobile (`grid grid-cols-2 gap-4`).
- **Signals (5 total):** Licensed · Insured · Locally Owned · Established [X] · Free Quotes.
  - Each signal: Lucide icon (`strokeWidth={2}`) in white (`text-white`), label below in DM Sans weight 500 `text-slate-200 text-xs md:text-sm`.
- **Dividers:** Cyan vertical accent dividers between signals on desktop: `border-r border-r-cyan-400/40` on items 1–4 (none on item 5). Mobile drops dividers (signals stack as flex children with gap).
- **No padding on parent section** — the Trust Strip floats over Hero's bottom edge via the negative margin.

## Services

- **Tone:** LIGHT.
- **Background:** `bg-slate-50`.
- **Vertical padding:** `py-20 md:py-24 lg:py-28` (extra top padding to compensate for the Trust Strip overlap).
- **Header cluster (max-w-3xl mb-12 md:mb-16):**
  - **Accent bar:** `h-1 w-12 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full mb-4` (cyan-500 chosen because the section bg is light — cyan-400 would wash out; cyan-500 sits with more weight).
  - Eyebrow uppercase tracking-wide `text-cyan-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-semibold` (cyan-600 on light bg per Visual Hard Rule #2 — the CTA accent owns the eyebrow).
  - H2: DM Serif Display weight 400, `text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl tracking-tight text-slate-900`. Explicit `text-slate-900` because base CSS rule sets `font-family` only.
  - Lead: DM Sans, `text-lg text-slate-600 max-w-prose`.
- **Card grid:** `grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8`.
- **Cards (8 total):**
  - Titles: `Service 1`, `Service 2`, …, `Service 8` (literal policy placeholders).
  - Body: ~12–15-word lorem ipsum each, DM Sans weight 400 `text-slate-600 leading-relaxed`.
  - Card title: DM Serif Display weight 400, `text-xl text-slate-900`.
  - Icon: Lucide icon (slate `text-cyan-600`) inside a tinted circle `bg-cyan-50 w-12 h-12 rounded-full grid place-items-center mb-4`.
  - **Card styling — pronounced shadow + cyan edge glow on hover (NO tilt):**
    - Rest: `bg-white rounded-xl p-6 shadow-[0_16px_48px_-12px_rgba(15,23,42,0.25)] ring-1 ring-slate-200/60 transition-all duration-300`.
    - Hover: `hover:shadow-[0_24px_64px_-12px_rgba(15,23,42,0.35)] hover:-translate-y-1 hover:ring-1 hover:ring-cyan-500/30`.
    - On hover, icon container fades to deeper cyan tint per Visual Hard Rule #2: `group-hover:bg-cyan-100 group-hover:text-cyan-700`.
  - **NO tilted-card treatment** — that was Template 3's visual mechanic. Template 4's mechanic is pronounced shadow + cyan-edge-glow on hover.
- **Toggle:** Default 3 visible (`idx < 3`); "See All Services" button below grid reveals the other 5. Button: `inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-cyan-600 underline underline-offset-4 font-medium hover:text-cyan-700`. State: `useState<boolean>(false)`.

