## ContactForm preview-mode message

The form is wired per `resend-form-prompt.md` (four spec files installed in Phase 2). `NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_MODE=preview` short-circuits the submit before any network call. The success-state copy reads:

> This form goes live when [Template 4] launches.

Tone: factual, no "thanks!" framing (no real submission happened).

## Template Build Content Policy sweep grep (HARD RULE end-of-Phase-2)

Run from project root:

```
grep -rE "Greenway|Marcus|Edison|Bridgewater|Apex|Mike S\.|Sarah K\.|Brian G\.|Tom \w+|Jennifer R\.|David T\." components/ app/ lib/ hooks/
```

**Expected: ZERO matches in code.** Matches only inside `PLACEHOLDERS.md` are fine — the template code itself must contain none.

## Imagery summary (every Unsplash subject pre-cleared)

All images are subjects from this approved taxonomy. **Bias every choice toward twilight / dusk / blue-hour / accent-lit scenes** to reinforce the Cinematic Nightscape mood (per Visual Hard Rule #3's "Lighting drama: sunset, golden hour, deep shadows, twilight" category):

- Architectural elements (columns, formal entryways, stone walls, pergolas, gazebos) — preferred lit at dusk
- Hardscape (paver patios, walkways, retaining walls, fire pits without surrounding seating) — preferred under accent lighting
- Water features (fountains, koi ponds without fish visible, reflecting pools) — preferred at twilight
- Formal/symmetrical compositions (topiary, parterre gardens) — golden hour ideal
- Lighting drama (sunset, twilight, blue-hour, architectural accent lighting on hardscape)
- Equipment / tools / branded service trucks (About image-half only) — lit workspace or dusk OK
- Raw materials (stone stockpile, gravel piles, mulch) — lit workspace OK

**Forbidden:** people (faces, bodies, silhouettes), animals (any), living plants as primary subject (flower close-ups, plain grass fields), close-up greenery without an architectural anchor, flat grass-only landscape shots per Visual Hard Rule #3.

Every Unsplash URL HEAD-checks 200 via `scripts/verify-images.mjs` (installed Phase 2). Every Unsplash render uses `ImageWithFallback`, never raw `next/image`.
